WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:05.220
<i>To save Tokunosuke, I started a Duel 
against both Droite and Gauche at the same time!</i>

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:08.370
<i>But for for some reason, Astral isn't showing himself.</i>

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:11.920
<i>Their attacks are coming one after the other!</i>

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.100
<i>This is bad! At this rate, I'll...</i>

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:16.990
Gagaga Gardna!

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.530
There's no point in trying to defend your Monster when you have no cards in your hand!

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.160
<i>No cards in my hand?</i>

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:27.550
<i>That's right!</i>

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:31.760
I activate the effect of Tasuke Knight in my Graveyard!

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.190
If this card is in my Graveyard while my Monster is attacked when I have no cards in my hand...

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.390
...I can Special Summon this card and end the battle this turn!

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:48.330
What did you say!?

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.180
The Monster's attack was stopped!

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.200
I managed to make it...

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.890
What a persistent bastard!

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.210
Alright, it's my turn.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.870
I have two Level Four Monsters on my field.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.670
If I can just manage to Summon Hope...

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:06.890
Astral!?

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.810
Now, it's your turn!

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.120
<i>If he's not here, I can't call out Hope!</i>

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:24.720
Yuma!

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.820
Where the hell are you looking?!

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.600
Be gone, Astral!

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.490
Yuma...

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:37.730
Hope!

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.760
Go back to Yuma! He needs you!

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.210
You think I'll just let you run away?!

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:55.290
Hope!

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.040
<i>Even if Hope isn't here...</i>

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.040
My turn! Draw!

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.420
<i>This card can't defeat their Monsters!</i>

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:13.190
I attack Phantom Butterfly Assassin Morpho with Tasuke Knight!

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:14.540
Hell Push!

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.560
Only 500 points?

00:02:23.270 --> 00:02:25.910
That ain't enough spirit to beat us!

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:30.670
Hope!

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.000
Go to Hell!

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:45.810
What's the matter, kid?

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.150
Hurry up and end your turn!

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:50.710
Yuma...

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.820
I'll put an end to this.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.350
Damn it!

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.830
I set a card face-down...

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:02.940
W-What!?

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.160
T-This is...

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.470
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.480
Why just Hope?

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.930
Astral... Are you here, Astral?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.530
Astral, did something happen to you?

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:32.080
So he got away, huh?

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:34.570
But Astral...

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:37.900
Now the only one who could defend you has left.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.200
The stupid fool left all so he could help out some lowly human.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.620
Now, come to me, Numbers!

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:49.290
I will absorb all of you myself!

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.040
The Numbers!

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.050
Now all of them are under my control!

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.970
And you're next, Astral.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.040
It's your turn!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.730
Wh-What was the deal with that light just now?

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.060
Something isn't right here.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:15.350
Be careful, Gauche!

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.690
It looks like the Hope card has returned!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:20.570
Astral...

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.360
Are you off fighting somewhere or something?

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:27.320
Thats why you sent him to me alone...?

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.580
If that's the case, I won't let your feelings go to waste!

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.230
I'll bring it to em!

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:39.990
I Overlay the Level Four Gagaga Gardna and Tasuke Knight!

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.910
I build the Overlay Network with my two Monsters!

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.800
Xyz Summon!

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:53.610
Appear, Number 39! Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.200
It's Hope!

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:58.790
He did it!

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.380
N-No way!

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.160
A Number?!

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:05.100
That kid has a Number!?

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.230
Number 39!?

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.740
Hope, endure it!

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:16.010
I set a card face-down and end my turn!

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.170
A Number...?

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:23.610
This thing's become far more interesting!

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:24.820
Calm down, Gauche!

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:27.840
My turn! Draw!

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.470
I Summon Moonlit Papillon!

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:36.420
Wait, Droite!

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:38.950
I already told you he's mine!

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:40.560
I can't allow that!

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:46.490
Now that we know he possesses a Number, this has become a Duel for Mr. Heartland!

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.570
You're such a killjoy!

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:55.810
I Overlay the Level Four Phantom Butterfly Assassin Swallowtail and Moonlit Papillon!

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:59.410
I build the Overlay Network with my two Monsters!

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:00.970
Xyz Summon!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.590
Appear, Photon Butterfly Assassin!

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:09.170
Photon!?

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.060
I've never seen such a Monster.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.280
This Monster is...

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:19.200
...the same type of Monsters Kaito used!

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:23.170
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:26.220
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:33.480
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:42.740
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:47.240
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:53.700
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:58.500
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:04.170
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:09.430
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:12.310
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:15.600
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:20.770
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:23.360
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:26.530
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:07:26.860 --> 00:07:32.080
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.580
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:37.580
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:44.380
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:55.620
Number 38: Connect the Hope Together! 
Hope Sword Mars Slash!!"

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.860
What? Photon Monsters just like Kaito?

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.370
Did you say Kaito?!

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.500
How do you know Kaito?

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.040
Just give it up!

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:06.290
Running away is useless!

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:11.170
I will force you to remember our mission.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.260
Why are you asking?!

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.390
It's obvious that I Dueled him!

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.140
It was quite a tiring match, too.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:19.180
What!?

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.060
You fought Kaito on even ground?!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.850
Why did Kaito fight this kid?

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:26.190
Could it be...

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.360
What Mr. Heartland told us about...?

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:35.360
That Original Number who came to this world from the Astral World?

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.790
Hey! Are you telling me this kid has the Original with him?!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:44.540
If not, how can you explain someone like him fighting Kaito evenly?

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.460
So that's the mood, is it?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.090
Since you seem to know the Original...

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.260
Kid, I'll be taking that Number back!

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.760
Let's begin the Number hunting!

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.350
Photon Butterfly Assassin's Monster Effect activates!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:06.900
By detaching one Overlay Unit, it switches a Defense Mode Monster into Attack Mode,

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.520
and its Attack Power goes down by 600!

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.860
Hope is in Attack Mode!?

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.280
Regardless of whether you have the spirit to fortify your defense, it won't work against us!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:22.240
Then I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Berserk Scales!

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:28.630
This raises the Attack Power of one Monster by 1000 points until the end of this turn!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.840
An Attack Power of 3100!?

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:35.090
Now the difference in their Attack Power is 1200 points.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:38.640
Even if the Number won't be destroyed, you'll still take damage!

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.890
Which means, once I take this attack...

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.980
Go, Photon Butterfly Assassin!

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.190
Attack Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:49.360
Butterfly Distortion!

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:54.690
Yuma!

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.160
Aspiring Emperor - Hope's Monster Effect activates!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:03.120
By detaching one Overlay Unit, it negates one Monster's attack!

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:04.870
Moon Barrier!

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:09.500
I'm saved!

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.500
With this I end my turn.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:20.050
The Monster that has used Berserk Scales' effect has its Attack Power returned to normal with 1000 more points decreased.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.770
But by doing this, we now know Aspiring Emperor - Hope's effect.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:25.810
Gauche!

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.310
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.900
Allow me to show you some <i>real</i> spirit!

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.860
My turn! Draw!

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:41.490
I release the Level Four Blade Bouncer to Advance Summon the Level Six Phantom Bouncer!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.910
Two Level Six Monsters!?

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:52.880
I Overlay the Level Six Hammer Rush Bouncer and Phantom Bouncer!

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.210
I build the Overlay Network with my two Monsters!

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:58.760
Xyz Summon!

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:03.350
Appear, Photon Streak Bouncer!

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:08.560
An Attack Power of 2700!?

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.060
Now it's over!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:14.940
Photon Streak Bouncer attacks Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:18.070
Take this! Streak Strike!

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.490
Aspiring Emperor - Hope's Monster Effect activates!

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.370
Moon Barrier!

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.200
You fell for it!

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:28.080
What!?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.000
Photon Streak Bouncer's effect activates!

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:38.380
By detaching one Overlay Unit, it negates the opponent's Xyz Monster's effect and deals 1000 points of damage!

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:42.800
So he wanted me to use Hope's effect for this!?

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:47.890
So instead of you taking 800 points, you'll take an additional 1000 points on top of it!

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.310
This is over!

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:57.440
Yuma?

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.950
Now I've got you, Astral.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:12.790
You're done for.

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.250
Go, Photon Streak Bouncer!

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.380
Streak Break!!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.850
Trap activate! Damage Diet!

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.890
It halves all damage done to me during this turn!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:43.860
Yuma!

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:49.200
Not done yet! Since Hope's effect has been negated, the battle resumes!

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:52.870
Do it, Photon Streak Bouncer!

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.090
Yuma's about to lose!

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.380
Now the Original Number belongs to me!

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.680
Trap, activate! Half Unbreak!

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:11.560
The Monster that has used this effect can't be destroyed by battle this turn!

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.600
And the damage to the player is halved!

00:13:26.110 --> 00:13:27.610
So you managed to withstand it.

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:34.580
But now Hope's Overlay Units and your set cards are gone.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:37.750
Stand up.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:42.170
Then surrender and hand us your Number.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.050
If you do that, you'll no longer have to suffer.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:48.300
Stop kidding me!

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.970
As if I'm gonna surrender to people like you!

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:55.730
Y-Yuma...

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:57.440
That's right.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:04.070
If I lose this Duel, I'm not the only one affected. He'll disappear!

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:07.240
I won't let such a thing happen!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:12.700
I set a card face-down and end my turn!

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.290
My turn! Draw!

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.420
I Summon Card Car D!

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:28.130
By releasing this card during the turn the card is Summoned,

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.600
I can draw two cards from my deck!

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:37.940
Please give me some cards to turn the tables!

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.990
Double Up Chance and Bi-Tension?

00:14:48.570 --> 00:14:49.570
These cards are...

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.160
No, think about it...

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.000
Just think. There has to be a way.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.630
There's gotta be a chance here...

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.590
Something...!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:11.760
What's wrong!?

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:16.100
My, my. So he finally gave up?

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:21.400
Yuma...

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:23.520
So he gave up?

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.650
Guess I'll finish you off as well.

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:33.450
Yuma...

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.830
It's useless...

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.550
Astral... I'm...

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.130
Don't give up!

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:53.090
This isn't how you Duel, Yuma!

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:54.220
That's right!

00:15:55.100 --> 00:16:00.430
No matter how much you failed, no matter how much you were laughed at... You never gave up, Yuma!

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.150
Don't give up until the very end!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:04.400
Bring it to em'!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.150
Kotori... Tokunosuke...

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:13.530
That's right, huh? The match isn't over yet.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.200
I can't let myself give up!

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.580
I'll win no matter what it takes!

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:21.370
I'll bring it to em'!

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:36.550
Yuma, I can feel it.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.600
You're bringing it to em'!

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:46.440
What is this?

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.650
My body's been paralyzed!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.950
This is Yuma and I's...

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:57.320
It's the power of our bonds!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.280
Bonds, you say!?

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:13.630
Yuma...!

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.180
You're... Astral!

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.430
I've kept you waiting.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:24.810
What is that?

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:26.190
Astral!

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.770
It's Astral!

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.730
I see! He's The Original!

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.990
It's not like I needed you or anything!

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:41.950
I could've beaten those guys by myself!

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.660
And you just had to vanish when I needed to feel your presence!

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:47.040
You went off somewhere!

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:49.380
<i>Both of them against Yuma...</i>

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.340
The pieces to victory are gathered!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.590
Your battle wasn't useless.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.220
Astral...

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.310
Yuma... Let's win.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:03.430
Right!

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:09.230
Here I go! First I activate the effect of Overlay Eater in the Graveyard!

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:13.360
I activate the effect of Overlay Eater in my Graveyard!

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.110
Overlay Eater?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:21.410
He sent it to the Graveyard to activate the effect of Gagaga Gardna before!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.660
I Banish this card in my Graveyard from the game!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:29.580
It absorbs one of the opponent's Xyz Monster's Overlay Units,

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:33.500
and makes it my own Xyz Monster's Overlay Unit!

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:40.090
Now Photon Streak Bouncer's effect has been stopped!

00:18:40.510 --> 00:18:43.260
Even if you're that fired up, it's way too late!

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:48.270
Aspiring Emperor - Hope, attack Photon Butterfly Assassin!

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:51.270
Even so, it's only 800 points of damage!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:54.270
Aspiring Emperor - Hope's Monster Effect activates!

00:18:54.820 --> 00:18:57.320
It negates one Monster's attack!

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:59.910
Negating your own attack!?

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:04.330
From my hand, I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Double Up Chance!

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:13.420
If a Monster's attack was negated, that Monster can attack once more with its Attack Power doubled!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.340
Hope's Attack Power doubled!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:19.470
But it's still not enough.

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:24.810
Then, from my hand I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Bi-Tension!

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:30.640
If a Monster attacks more than once, its Attack Power is doubled once more!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.900
7600 Attack Points?!

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:34.860
What!?

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.320
Let's go, Yuma!

00:19:36.570 --> 00:19:37.030
Right!

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:41.200
Hope Sword Mars Slash!!

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:49.830
Trap, activate! Bouncer Guard!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:54.840
It switches a Monster's Attack Target to a Monster with "Bouncer" in its name!

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:14.940
You did it!

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:16.650
He won, Yuma won!

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:18.440
That was amazing!

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:20.820
In that situation, he managed to do a counter-attack!

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:24.450
Astral really is a Dueling genius after all!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.370
Listen, you...

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:29.040
Why did you defend me?

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:31.500
Heh, why?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.420
I was just in the mood to.

00:20:33.420 --> 00:20:35.210
Am I wrong?

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.250
But Astral really is something else.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:37.210
Hey kid!

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:40.920
As promised, we'll forget about your cheating friend.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:45.340
But you better remember that I'm gonna beat you next time!

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:48.310
Along with the Original Number!

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:55.100
Interesting! I'll be your opponent anytime!

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:58.940
I like that spirit of yours.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.570
Well, what's done is done.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:07.160
The rest is gonna be a breeze for me!

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:09.910
Found you!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.290
How dare you trick us!

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:14.210
Return my Heart Piece!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:17.460
Hold it right there!

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:27.590
Let's go, everyone!

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.230
That was really harsh!

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:36.940
G-Gone!

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:42.780
My Heart Pieces... are gone!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:47.910
Droite, don't report what happened today to Mr. Heartland!

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:48.950
What?

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:51.200
I'll defeat that Original!

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:53.160
Before Kaito does!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:57.370
Fine then...

00:22:00.790 --> 00:22:02.050
It's gone...

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:06.680
Please let him have dropped my Heart Piece somewhere!

00:22:07.050 --> 00:22:08.930
Cleaning, Cleaning...

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:23.070
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:28.990
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.910
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:37.960
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:41.540
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:45.630
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:48.430
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:52.890
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:55.930
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.430 --> 00:22:59.230
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:06.320
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:09.360
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.610 --> 00:23:13.830
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:14.030 --> 00:23:15.790
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:17.580
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:22.960
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:26.000
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:29.590
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:34.010
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:35.850
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:38.140
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>
